# The SynapseOS release signing key.
#
# A fingerprint is public — it is what people are told to check the ISO
# against, and it is on soslinux.org. Nothing secret lives here; the key
# itself is in the release box's keyring and nowhere else.
#
# This file exists so that signing is NAMED without anyone having to remember
# to name it. gpg --detach-sign with no -u picks the first usable secret key,
# and a release signed with somebody's personal identity is not something you
# can quietly take back — so the choice is written down once, in the repo,
# rather than typed into an environment variable per build.
#
# Rotating the key: change the line below, publish the new public key on
# soslinux.org, and keep the old one published — the ISOs it signed are still
# out there.
#
# SynapseOS Release Signing <releases@soslinux.org>  ed25519, expires 2029-08-28
65489EF5C20D0BD94211472BED336DB7952B609E
